  <section id="leadership" class="section leadership-section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="kicker">Leadership in practice</p>
      <h2>Clear decisions. Aligned teams. Measurable outcomes.</h2>
      <p>My role is to create clarity, focus resources, and help people deliver work that matters.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="leadership-grid">
      <article><span>01</span><h3>Set direction</h3><p>Turn complex business and technical needs into clear priorities and a practical path forward.</p></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>Align people and resources</h3><p>Bring stakeholders together, build on proven capabilities, and focus investment where it creates the most value.</p></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>Deliver measurable outcomes</h3><p>Build responsibly, validate the complete solution, and measure whether it works for the business and its users.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="work" class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="kicker">Selected work</p>
      <h2>See these principles applied in working systems.</h2>
      <p>These projects show how I turn technical direction into working software, clear safeguards, and measurable release decisions.</p>
    </div>

    <article class="project featured">
      <div class="project-number">01</div>
      <div class="project-body">
        <div class="project-meta"><span>Physical AI</span><span>Release validation</span><span>2026</span></div>
        <h3>Robot Release Gate</h3>
        <p class="project-lede">Test how the machine behaves—not just whether the code runs.</p>
        <p>A deterministic prototype where an AI-runtime update passes component checks but adds 180 ms of decision latency. The robot misses its pickup, so the deployment is blocked on physical outcome.</p>
        <div class="project-proof">
          <div><span class="pass">PASS</span><small>model equivalence</small></div>
          <div><span class="pass">PASS</span><small>throughput</small></div>
          <div><span class="fail">BLOCK</span><small>task completion</small></div>
        </div>
        <p class="scope-note"><strong>Honest boundary:</strong> this is a browser-based timing experiment, not a physics simulation or hardware validation. The next test is reproducing the failure in MuJoCo.</p>
        <div class="project-links">
          <a href="https://tryambak2019.github.io/physical-ai-release-gate/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View live experiment ↗</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/tryambak2019/physical-ai-release-gate" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Inspect source ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="project">
      <div class="project-number">02</div>
      <div class="project-body">
        <div class="project-meta"><span>Agent infrastructure</span><span>BigQuery</span><span>Google Cloud</span></div>
        <h3>SQL Execution Gate</h3>
        <p class="project-lede">An agent that must show its work before it can touch data.</p>
        <p>A deployed, safety-gated BigQuery assistant that separates SQL planning from execution. It loads the live schema, exposes generated SQL for an explicit human decision, mechanically blocks standard SQL writes, and fails closed when execution errors.</p>
        <ul class="compact-list">
          <li>Planner and tool-bearing executor are separate agents.</li>
          <li>Human approve/reject gate stays in the same session.</li>
          <li>React, FastAPI, Google ADK, Terraform, Cloud Build, and Cloud Run.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="project-links">
          <a href="https://fsbq-agent-bqjiefengq-uc.a.run.app/app/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open live demo ↗</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/tryambak2019/sql-execution-gate" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Inspect architecture and source ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="project">
      <div class="project-number">03</div>
      <div class="project-body">
        <div class="project-meta"><span>Coursework portfolio</span><span>Deep learning</span><span>2019–2022</span></div>
        <h3>AISC project archive, rebuilt as a verifiable portfolio</h3>
        <p class="project-lede">Original third-party publication links disappeared, so the work is now documented under my own site and source repositories.</p>
        <p>This collection includes recommender systems, reinforcement learning, generative modeling, semi-supervised learning, anomaly detection, NLP, and MLOps work. Large/private assets are intentionally excluded and mapped to reproducible or public sources.</p>
        <div class="project-links">
          <a href="/aisc/">View AISC portfolio pages ↗</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/tryambak2019/AISC" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Inspect curated repo ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
